{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-ac023fc9a5048e02", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# TS3-Codec: Transformer-Based Simple Streaming Single Codec\narXiv: 2411.18803\nAuthors: Haibin Wu, Naoyuki Kanda, Sefik Emre Eskimez, Jinyu Li\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of TS3-Codec, the first purely transformer-based and convolution-free neural audio codec.\n  2. Demonstration that the transformer-only architecture achieves comparable or superior performance to convolution-based codecs while requiring only 12% of the computation and 77% of the bitrate.\n  3. Demonstration that the proposed architecture significantly outperforms convolution-based codecs when using similar computational resources.\n  4. Development of the first single-codebook neural audio codec specifically designed for streaming capability.\n  5. Exploration of single-codebook designs with large codebook sizes of 65k and 130k.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VQ", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "93a78959-3133-4567-b8dc-29dbc81e853a", "uuid": "1297cfda-62c5-4c22-8d3a-142b954d3143", "timestamp": "2026-07-28T08:09:53.778Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# TS3-Codec: Transformer-Based Simple Streaming Single Codec\narXiv: 2411.18803\nAuthors: Haibin Wu, Naoyuki Kanda, Sefik Emre Eskimez, Jinyu Li\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of TS3-Codec, the first purely transformer-based and convolution-free neural audio codec.\n  2. Demonstration that the transformer-only architecture achieves comparable or superior performance to convolution-based codecs while requiring only 12% of the computation and 77% of the bitrate.\n  3. Demonstration that the proposed architecture significantly outperforms convolution-based codecs when using similar computational resources.\n  4. Development of the first single-codebook neural audio codec specifically designed for streaming capability.\n  5. Exploration of single-codebook designs with large codebook sizes of 65k and 130k.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VQ", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
