{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bdf1aac187df95ef", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Fish Audio S2 Technical Report\narXiv: 2603.08823\nAuthors: Shijia Liao, Yuxuan Wang, Songting Liu, Yifan Cheng, Ruoyi Zhang, Tianyu Li, Shidong Li, Yisheng Zheng, Xingwei Liu, Qingzheng Wang, Zhizhuo Zhou, Jiahua Liu, Xin Chen, Dawei Han\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A Dual-AR architecture that decouples temporal semantic modeling from depth-wise acoustic generation for efficient high-fidelity speech synthesis.\n  2. A dual-purpose data pipeline where speech quality and rich-transcription ASR models serve as both pre-training data filters and RL reward signals to eliminate distribution shift.\n  3. An RL-based post-training method using GRPO with multi-dimensional rewards to jointly optimize semantic accuracy, acoustic quality, and speaker similarity.\n  4. Native support for multi-speaker, multi-turn dialogue generation and stable long-form coherent audio synthesis.\n  5. Enhanced zero-shot instruction-following capabilities enabling fine-grained control over speech generation via natural language descriptions and inline vocal tags.\n  6. A production-ready SGLang-based inference engine achieving an RTF of 0.195 and a time-to-first-audio below 100 ms.\n  7. The introduction of the Fish Audio Instruction Benchmark to systematically evaluate fine-grained inline tag-following performance in TTS models.\n  8. The open-source release of the model weights, fine-tuning code, and inference engine to facilitate future TTS research.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/控制-指令合成, TTS/功能-多说话人", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "93a78959-3133-4567-b8dc-29dbc81e853a", "uuid": "ed768e61-a435-4279-b768-4e24e3dbe2ad", "timestamp": "2026-07-28T08:09:54.290Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Fish Audio S2 Technical Report\narXiv: 2603.08823\nAuthors: Shijia Liao, Yuxuan Wang, Songting Liu, Yifan Cheng, Ruoyi Zhang, Tianyu Li, Shidong Li, Yisheng Zheng, Xingwei Liu, Qingzheng Wang, Zhizhuo Zhou, Jiahua Liu, Xin Chen, Dawei Han\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A Dual-AR architecture that decouples temporal semantic modeling from depth-wise acoustic generation for efficient high-fidelity speech synthesis.\n  2. A dual-purpose data pipeline where speech quality and rich-transcription ASR models serve as both pre-training data filters and RL reward signals to eliminate distribution shift.\n  3. An RL-based post-training method using GRPO with multi-dimensional rewards to jointly optimize semantic accuracy, acoustic quality, and speaker similarity.\n  4. Native support for multi-speaker, multi-turn dialogue generation and stable long-form coherent audio synthesis.\n  5. Enhanced zero-shot instruction-following capabilities enabling fine-grained control over speech generation via natural language descriptions and inline vocal tags.\n  6. A production-ready SGLang-based inference engine achieving an RTF of 0.195 and a time-to-first-audio below 100 ms.\n  7. The introduction of the Fish Audio Instruction Benchmark to systematically evaluate fine-grained inline tag-following performance in TTS models.\n  8. The open-source release of the model weights, fine-tuning code, and inference engine to facilitate future TTS research.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/控制-指令合成, TTS/功能-多说话人", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a6fa0c2ff6b9f7c0", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# High Fidelity Neural Audio Compression\narXiv: 2210.13438\nAuthors: Alexandre Défossez, Jade Copet, Gabriel Synnaeve, Yossi Adi\nYear: 2022 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a state-of-the-art real-time, high-fidelity neural audio codec using a streaming encoder-decoder architecture with quantized latent space.\n  2. Simplification and acceleration of training by using a single multiscale spectrogram adversary that efficiently reduces artifacts and produces high-quality samples.\n  3. Introduction of a novel loss balancer mechanism that stabilizes training by defining loss weights as the fraction of the overall gradient they represent, decoupling them from the natural scale of the loss.\n  4. Demonstration that lightweight Transformer models can further compress the representation by up to 40% while remaining faster than real time.\n  5. Superiority of the proposed approach over baseline methods across all evaluated settings, including both 24 kHz monophonic and 48 kHz stereophonic audio.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-声学", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "93a78959-3133-4567-b8dc-29dbc81e853a", "uuid": "ddebaf8e-6c83-41c1-9d36-df5e356fe2cd", "timestamp": "2026-07-28T08:09:54.537Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# High Fidelity Neural Audio Compression\narXiv: 2210.13438\nAuthors: Alexandre Défossez, Jade Copet, Gabriel Synnaeve, Yossi Adi\nYear: 2022 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a state-of-the-art real-time, high-fidelity neural audio codec using a streaming encoder-decoder architecture with quantized latent space.\n  2. Simplification and acceleration of training by using a single multiscale spectrogram adversary that efficiently reduces artifacts and produces high-quality samples.\n  3. Introduction of a novel loss balancer mechanism that stabilizes training by defining loss weights as the fraction of the overall gradient they represent, decoupling them from the natural scale of the loss.\n  4. Demonstration that lightweight Transformer models can further compress the representation by up to 40% while remaining faster than real time.\n  5. Superiority of the proposed approach over baseline methods across all evaluated settings, including both 24 kHz monophonic and 48 kHz stereophonic audio.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-声学", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
